  <p>You can sell Procreate brushes on Gumroad. Create a digital product, upload your <code>.brush</code> or <code>.brushset</code> files, set a price, and publish. Your buyers pay on your product page, download the files, and open them in Procreate.</p>
  <p>You don't need your own website. Gumroad gives your product a page with its own link, takes the payment, and delivers the files to each buyer.</p>

  <h3 id="export-brushes">Export your brushes from Procreate</h3>
  <p>Procreate saves one brush as a <code>.brush</code> file and a whole brush set as a <code>.brushset</code> file. For most products, sell a <code>.brushset</code> file, because your buyer gets every brush in the set from one file.</p>
  <p>To export from Procreate on your iPad:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the Brush Library.</li>
    <li>Share the brush set, or the single brush, that you want to sell.</li>
    <li>Save the file to the Files app.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Procreate's menus change between versions. If these steps don't match what you see, check Procreate's own help pages.</p>
  <p>Give each file a name your buyers will recognize, such as <code>ink-and-pencil.brushset</code>.</p>

  <h3 id="create-product">Create your product</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>On your <a href="https://gumroad.com/products">Products dashboard</a>, click <strong>New product</strong>.</li>
    <li>Enter a <strong>Name</strong>, such as "Ink and pencil brushes for Procreate".</li>
    <li>Under Products, choose <strong>Digital product</strong>.</li>
    <li>Enter a <strong>Price</strong>.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Next: Customize</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Gumroad opens the product editor on the Product tab. Add two things there:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>A <strong>Description</strong>. Say how many brushes are in the set, what they are for, and which version of Procreate you made them in.</li>
    <li>A <strong>Cover</strong>. You can add up to 8 images or videos. Show strokes drawn with each brush, so people can see what they are buying. See <a href="60-adding-a-cover-image">Adding cover and thumbnail images</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Then click <strong>Save and continue</strong>.</p>

  <h3 id="upload-files">Upload your brush files</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the <strong>Content</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Upload your files</strong>, then <strong>Computer files</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose your brush files. You can choose several at once.</li>
    <li>When the uploads finish, click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If the page already has content, click <strong>Upload files</strong> in the toolbar instead.</p>
  <p>Each file can be up to 20 GB, and you can add as many files as you want. Free products have a lower limit. See <a href="289-file-size-limits-on-gumroad">File size limits</a>.</p>
  <p>How you package the files changes what your buyers have to do:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>One <code>.brushset</code> file for each set.</strong> A buyer on an iPad downloads the set and opens it in Procreate. They don't unzip anything. Use this for most products.</li>
    <li><strong>A zip file of the whole pack.</strong> Your buyer gets every set in one download, and unzips it before opening the files. This suits large packs, and buyers who download on a computer.</li>
    <li><strong>A folder.</strong> On the Content tab, drag files onto each other to group them into a folder. Your buyers see a Download all button on the folder when its files total less than 500 MB. Download all gives them a zip file.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can combine these. Upload each set as its own file, and add a zip file of the whole pack below them.</p>

  <h3 id="install-steps">Tell your buyers how to install the brushes</h3>
  <p>After they pay, your buyers get a receipt email with a View content button. The button opens your product's content page, where each file has a Download button. Buyers with a Gumroad account also find the product in their <a href="247-what-your-customers-see">Library</a>.</p>
  <p>The text you type on the Content tab appears on the content page too. Write short install steps above your files. For example:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open this page in Safari on your iPad.</li>
    <li>Tap Download next to the brush set.</li>
    <li>Open the Files app, and tap the file you downloaded. Procreate opens and imports the brushes.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Then make a <a href="62-testing-a-purchase">test purchase</a> on an iPad, and follow your own steps. Correct them if anything differs.</p>
  <p>If you include a zip file, tell your buyers to unzip it first. <a href="206-how-to-open-zip-and-rar-files">How to open ZIP and RAR files</a> has steps for Mac, PC, and mobile devices.</p>
  <p>The Gumroad mobile app opens audio, video, PDF, and EPUB files. Brush files are not among the <a href="112-mobile-friendly-files">mobile-friendly files</a>, so send your buyers to the content page in their browser.</p>

  <h3 id="pricing">Choose how to price your brushes</h3>
  <p>Set the price in the <strong>Amount</strong> field on the Product tab. You can also use these pricing options:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pay what you want.</strong> Turn on Allow customers to pay what they want, under the Amount field. The Amount becomes the lowest price a buyer can pay. See <a href="133-pay-what-you-want-pricing">"Pay what you want" pricing</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>A free sample set.</strong> Create a second product with a few of your brushes, and set its Amount to 0. Gumroad turns on pay what you want for a free product, so buyers can take it for free or choose to pay. Link to your paid set in the description.</li>
    <li><strong>A bundle.</strong> A bundle sells two or more of your existing products for one price. See <a href="339-product-bundles">Product bundles</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>A discount code.</strong> Give your followers a lower price at launch without changing the Amount. See <a href="128-discount-codes">Discount codes</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="licenses">Sell personal and commercial licenses</h3>
  <p>Use versions to sell the same brushes under different licenses, at different prices.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the Product tab, and scroll to Versions.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Add version</strong>. Name the version "Personal use", and leave its <strong>Additional amount</strong> at 0.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Add version</strong> again. Name this version "Commercial use", and enter the extra price as its <strong>Additional amount</strong>.</li>
    <li>Save your changes.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>A buyer pays the Amount plus the Additional amount of the version they choose. Write what each license allows in the version's Description, and in your product description.</p>
  <p>To give a version its own files, such as a license PDF, go to the Content tab and open the version menu at the top. Uncheck Use the same content for all versions, then choose the version to edit. See <a href="126-setting-up-versions-on-a-digital-product">Setting up versions</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="discover">Add a category and tags for Gumroad Discover</h3>
  <p><a href="79-gumroad-discover">Gumroad Discover</a> is Gumroad's marketplace. A category and tags help buyers who search or browse there find your brushes.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the <strong>Share</strong> tab, and scroll to Gumroad Discover.</li>
    <li>In <strong>Category</strong>, type "Procreate", and choose Drawing &amp; Painting &gt; Digital Illustration &gt; Illustration Brushes &gt; Procreate.</li>
    <li>In <strong>Tags</strong>, add up to 10 tags. Each tag must be 2 to 20 characters long. As you type, Gumroad suggests tags and shows how many products use each one.</li>
    <li>Keep "Display your product's 1-5 star rating to prospective customers" turned on.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Use the words your buyers search with, such as "procreate brushes", "lettering", or "watercolor".</p>
  <p>Your product can appear on Discover once it has a category, shows its rating, and has made at least one sale. Your account has to be eligible too. See <a href="79-gumroad-discover#Discover-eligibility-OtTcp">Discover eligibility</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="publish">Publish and share your product</h3>
  <p>On the Share tab, click <strong>Publish</strong>. Then click <strong>Copy URL</strong> to copy your product's link, and share it with your followers.</p>
  <p>You need a payout method before you can publish. Add one in your <a href="260-your-payout-settings-page">payout settings</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="update-brushes">How do I update a brush set for past buyers?</h3>
  <p>Replace the file on the product. Buyers who already own the product get the new file on their content page, and they don't pay again.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the Content tab.</li>
    <li>Remove the old file, and upload the new one.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If the product has sales, Gumroad asks "Would you like to notify your customers about those changes?" Click <strong>Send notification</strong> to open an email to your buyers, with the title and message started for you. See <a href="169-how-to-send-an-update">Send email updates</a> for what you need before you can send emails.</p>

  <h3 id="refunds">Do I have to offer refunds on brushes?</h3>
  <p>You choose your own refund policy. You can allow no refunds, or offer a money back guarantee of 7 days, 14 days, 30 days, or 6 months. See <a href="335-custom-refund-policy">Set a custom refund policy</a>.</p>
  <p>Whatever you choose, Gumroad can refund a sale within 90 days of purchase to prevent a chargeback. See <a href="51-what-is-gumroads-refund-policy">Gumroad's refund policy</a>.</p>
  <p>After a full refund, the buyer can no longer open the content page. To refund a sale yourself, see <a href="47-how-to-refund-a-customer">Issuing a refund</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="fees">How much does Gumroad charge?</h3>
  <p>Gumroad charges 10% + $0.50 on each sale, plus payment processing. Card processing is 2.9% + $0.30. Sales that come from Gumroad Discover have a flat 30% fee instead, which includes processing.</p>
  <p>Gumroad has no monthly fee. See <a href="66-gumroads-fees">Gumroad's fees</a>.</p>
